I'm just looking to see what, what Pac-Man was up to in 1990.

00:36:34.100 --> 00:36:38.220
Like maybe, maybe they actually released too many bad games by then that they were like,

00:36:38.300 --> 00:36:39.920
there's no way we could put out another Pac-Man game.

00:36:40.020 --> 00:36:41.060
Like people are dumb with him.

00:36:41.800 --> 00:36:44.880
But that just doesn't seem, I don't know.

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:46.020
That doesn't feel true.

00:36:46.300 --> 00:36:47.500
Right? It doesn't.

00:36:48.140 --> 00:36:55.320
Pac-Mania came out in 1987 and that was like that weird 3D one where, um, he's still, he's

00:36:55.320 --> 00:36:56.420
still a giant sphere.

00:36:56.660 --> 00:37:01.000
He doesn't have like, uh, in the, in the promotional posters, he still has his arms and legs, but

00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:02.220
not in the game. Thankfully.

00:37:02.220 --> 00:37:07.120
I don't think you would have the arms and legs in the game until the, the Pac world games.

00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:08.700
Yes. Yeah.

00:37:08.760 --> 00:37:12.220
Let's see. The next Pac-Man game is pro, yeah.

00:37:12.580 --> 00:37:15.180
Looks like Pac-Attack.

00:37:15.400 --> 00:37:21.080
This is now a, uh, save Pac-Man symposium.

00:37:21.080 --> 00:37:24.760
We're no longer talking about rock and ball.

00:37:25.100 --> 00:37:27.340
Well, here's the crazy thing about the next Pac-Man game.

00:37:27.460 --> 00:37:30.300
Okay. It's Pac-Attack, which is a Tetris game.

00:37:30.420 --> 00:37:32.680
All right. It's a, it's Tetris, but with Pac-Man.

00:37:32.900 --> 00:37:38.960
So they think that's fine to send to America, but do not send pinball with Pac-Man.

00:37:38.960 --> 00:37:40.700
Well, yeah, because pinball stands on its own.

00:37:41.040 --> 00:37:42.460
All video gamers love pinball.

00:37:42.660 --> 00:37:43.980
Who's ever even heard of Tetris?

00:37:44.580 --> 00:37:51.360
Yeah. And like, I would get confused if my pinball, which is also a sphere, were to look like

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:52.640
a cute Pac-Man.

00:37:52.980 --> 00:38:01.700
Uh, I would be upset with the, the, like the analogy, um, that would just make me irate

00:38:01.700 --> 00:38:02.880
as I played the game.

00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:07.620
And the thing about the, the pinball ball, marble, whatever it is, is that it's a solid

00:38:07.620 --> 00:38:08.960
color. So it can be rolling.

00:38:09.200 --> 00:38:11.780
If it's Pac-Man, like he's got like a mouth and an eye.

00:38:11.780 --> 00:38:16.920
Okay. So like, if he's rolling, you need to see that, like, you can't just have him being

00:38:16.920 --> 00:38:18.560
like a solid Pac-Man moving around.

00:38:18.700 --> 00:38:20.160
That isn't like a ball rolling anymore.

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:21.880
No, it doesn't.

00:38:22.200 --> 00:38:26.900
And see, I played family pinball, uh, just to see what the Pac-Man elements were.

00:38:26.960 --> 00:38:29.140
And I was kind of surprised that Pac-Man wasn't the ball.

00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:31.660
Why wouldn't he just be the ball?

00:38:31.740 --> 00:38:34.120
It's not like, you know, it's not like you also have to have the ghost roaming the screen

00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:39.380
or something, or, you know, they didn't really make it look like a Pac-Man maze or anything

00:38:39.380 --> 00:38:40.540
like that. They didn't go crazy.

00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:44.440
It's not a complete. Redesign from the regular pinball that we have in this game.

00:38:44.780 --> 00:38:45.800
But I don't know.

00:38:46.260 --> 00:38:47.360
Like you said, Pac-Man's a sphere.

00:38:47.680 --> 00:38:49.580
Make him the ball. That would have been another nice touch.

00:38:49.620 --> 00:38:50.640
So Namco missed.

00:38:50.820 --> 00:38:56.480
You can have a mode in this game where the whole pinball machine is covered in pellets

00:38:56.480 --> 00:38:57.680
or dots or whatever they are.

00:38:57.840 --> 00:39:02.460
And you have to try and scoop them all up as many as you can by hitting Pac-Man into

00:39:02.460 --> 00:39:08.200
them. I just feel like whether it was the Japanese version or the American version, Namco made

00:39:08.200 --> 00:39:10.480
a misstep on both, on both accounts.

00:39:10.480 --> 00:39:11.920
I agree.

00:39:12.240 --> 00:39:14.700
And I think they should not be forgiven.

00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:20.140
But you see, they weren't the publishers in the North American one.

00:39:20.140 --> 00:39:22.860
So NTVIC was.

00:39:23.120 --> 00:39:24.380
And I don't even know. I've never heard of that.

00:39:24.880 --> 00:39:25.920
Yeah, that's the reason.

00:39:26.080 --> 00:39:30.380
But I'm saying like, so they bought the game off of Namco and we're like, yeah, we know

00:39:30.380 --> 00:39:35.000
we can't use Pac-Man, but we're gonna reskin the whole game.

00:39:35.100 --> 00:39:39.620
We just want to own the rights to this pinball game that you made and remove all mentions

00:39:39.620 --> 00:39:41.640
of Pac-Man. It just sounds like a crazy pitch.

00:39:42.120 --> 00:39:47.860
Maybe it was just like on sale if you didn't take the Pac-Man license, you know?

00:39:48.140 --> 00:39:50.300
Like I know this for a fact, actually.

00:39:50.640 --> 00:39:54.300
Joe, I've been trying to look up what they call the pinball ball because you raised a

00:39:54.300 --> 00:39:55.200
good point about it.

00:39:56.500 --> 00:39:58.280
But I don't have an answer for you, though.

00:39:58.420 --> 00:39:59.680
It's not something. Is it not just a pinball?

00:40:00.200 --> 00:40:02.180
Right. I would think it was called the pinball.

00:40:02.320 --> 00:40:05.280
But then I didn't want to sound stupid and be like, actually, no, it's just the whole

00:40:05.280 --> 00:40:07.180
machine is the pinball.

00:40:07.680 --> 00:40:09.440
And the ball is a marble.

00:40:09.720 --> 00:40:10.720
It's the pin. I can't tell you.

00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:17.440
Well, we all know that like a base, like the ball we use in baseball is actually called

00:40:17.440 --> 00:40:21.280
the pigeon. I always thought, well, the baseball is the field, right?

00:40:21.640 --> 00:40:24.280
Well, you play it on a field, but you hit the pigeon.

00:40:24.280 --> 00:40:29.260
Yeah, yeah. You play on a field, which is called the baseball, right?

00:40:30.420 --> 00:40:31.860
Called the baseball field.

00:40:32.040 --> 00:40:33.060
But Joe, I do know what you're saying.

00:40:33.100 --> 00:40:33.960
So don't worry. I'm not.

00:40:34.080 --> 00:40:35.420
You don't have to explain it to me.

00:40:35.620 --> 00:40:37.600
I was joking. Yeah.

00:40:37.600 --> 00:40:38.500
Is he not joking?

00:40:38.620 --> 00:40:39.560
Okay. I thought he was joking.

00:40:39.580 --> 00:40:40.380
No, he is. He is. I know.

00:40:40.700 --> 00:40:41.760
I know what he's saying. All right.

00:40:41.880 --> 00:40:43.620
We're all in on this joke together, right?

00:40:44.400 --> 00:40:48.140
Right. See, yeah, because I'm in the glossary for pinball terms.

00:40:48.440 --> 00:40:54.260
And it's not when I get to the P, there's no like pinball referring to the ball.

00:40:54.680 --> 00:40:59.420
But pin game is another term for a pinball machine, according to the pinball glossary.

00:40:59.780 --> 00:41:01.400
Pin game. Hmm.

00:41:01.560 --> 00:41:03.260
I think it's just going to be. I think it's going to be called the.

00:41:03.360 --> 00:41:04.580
I think it's going to be called the marble, guys.

00:41:04.760 --> 00:41:06.140
I think it's going to be called the pinball.

00:41:06.460 --> 00:41:07.920
I would like to call it the pinball, too.

00:41:08.200 --> 00:41:09.860
But think about this, Sean.

00:41:09.860 --> 00:41:13.840
We don't call the football strictly the football.

00:41:14.040 --> 00:41:15.140
We sometimes call it the pigskin.

00:41:15.780 --> 00:41:17.520
I'm going to call it the pong ball.

00:41:19.440 --> 00:41:21.580
Yeah. I mean, sometimes we call it the rock.

00:41:23.040 --> 00:41:24.620
Yeah. The rock, the pigskin.

00:41:24.760 --> 00:41:26.320
And so I'm just going to say it's the pigeon.

00:41:26.840 --> 00:41:27.760
Okay. Now listen to this.

00:41:28.660 --> 00:41:32.680
Everybody's familiar with more complicated variants of pinball, such as like when you

00:41:32.680 --> 00:41:36.600
get the multi ball bonus and a bunch of other balls spill out from all over the place.

00:41:36.720 --> 00:41:41.020
And you try to keep those for as long as you can, because as long as two or more are there,

00:41:41.020 --> 00:41:43.240
you still have like technically an extra life on screen.

00:41:43.480 --> 00:41:45.120
Yeah. That's called multi ball.

00:41:45.620 --> 00:41:51.100
And the pinball glossary says when several balls are in play at one time.

00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:52.380
Now, hold on a minute.

00:41:52.560 --> 00:41:56.100
They're not saying when several pinballs are in play.

00:41:56.300 --> 00:41:57.240
So just the ball.

00:41:57.480 --> 00:41:58.400
It's just a ball.

00:41:59.040 --> 00:42:01.760
All right. I mean, it could also just be like single ball.

00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:03.640
Well, I think that the single ball.

00:42:03.700 --> 00:42:08.980
I think that this confirms that the ball in pinball is the base form of a ball.

00:42:09.220 --> 00:42:12.260
Every other type of ball is a variation on the ball in a pinball.

00:42:12.580 --> 00:42:13.580
Yeah. It's the platonic ideal. Yes.

00:42:13.840 --> 00:42:17.780
Of ball. We, I think we started this conversation at the 35 minute mark.

00:42:19.540 --> 00:42:20.700
I'm really happy.

00:42:20.960 --> 00:42:22.460
15 more minutes then. Yeah.

00:42:22.980 --> 00:42:27.300
You may not like it, but that's what a pinball ball is called.

00:42:27.560 --> 00:42:28.820
On the sequels and spinoff.

00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:33.580
Yeah. On the sequels and spinoff side, none.

00:42:33.900 --> 00:42:34.780
Absolutely none.

00:42:35.340 --> 00:42:40.980
I can't find anything about NTVIC, except for in the manual,

00:42:41.720 --> 00:42:45.420
their international corporation is located at 50 Rockefeller Plaza,

00:42:45.640 --> 00:42:47.440
which is pretty close, not the exact address,

00:42:47.800 --> 00:42:50.560
to where the Nintendo New York City store is today.

00:42:50.560 --> 00:42:51.580
And I just find that funny.

00:42:51.860 --> 00:42:52.800
That is funny.

00:42:53.240 --> 00:42:57.620
Ha. Not like laugh out loud funny because I'm not laughing, but.

00:42:58.100 --> 00:42:59.440
The joke gave a ha. Yeah, it was a ha.

00:42:59.820 --> 00:43:03.160
And then I had a real genuine laugh after that, but it was at my own joke.

00:43:04.120 --> 00:43:06.420
Yes. You know what is no joke?

00:43:06.660 --> 00:43:07.460
What? Joke.

00:43:07.460 --> 00:43:09.720
Because we have to be really serious about it,

00:43:10.020 --> 00:43:14.560
is when we vote for games on the essential games list.

00:43:17.560 --> 00:43:23.480
Rockin' Ball is video game pinball with a lot of different modes,

00:43:23.480 --> 00:43:25.380
and we've covered them at length here.

00:43:25.380 --> 00:43:29.280
I did appreciate the twist on pinball.

00:43:29.560 --> 00:43:32.460
So if you have like another player to play against,

00:43:32.600 --> 00:43:33.400
maybe not the computer,

00:43:33.540 --> 00:43:35.460
although the computer offers a fine experience

00:43:35.460 --> 00:43:37.600
and at some points can challenge you too.

00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:39.520
I just think that this is the kind of game

00:43:39.520 --> 00:43:41.620
that you want a friend to play along with you,

00:43:41.620 --> 00:43:45.740
so this way you have that competitive itch inside of you.

00:43:45.900 --> 00:43:47.680
That would definitely be true in the battle

00:43:47.680 --> 00:43:49.280
and in the sports pinball modes,

00:43:49.520 --> 00:43:51.800
the two highlights of this game.

00:43:51.800 --> 00:43:55.580
The regular pinball is just so lackluster and boring,

00:43:55.700 --> 00:43:57.200
and there's only one bonus mode,

00:43:57.320 --> 00:43:58.140
and it's very easy.

00:43:58.260 --> 00:43:59.400
You just shoot into a ramp,

00:43:59.440 --> 00:44:02.260
and then a car just goes out of control

00:44:02.260 --> 00:44:04.380
and just keeps like going up and down and up and down,

00:44:04.560 --> 00:44:06.000
eating its way through the board

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:09.560
until you move into the bonus mode,

00:44:09.560 --> 00:44:13.020
which is just hitting a bunch of people to score points.

00:44:13.100 --> 00:44:15.360
My point being is just that the regular pinball,

00:44:15.520 --> 00:44:18.180
which is what the game is trying to sell you the idea on,

00:44:18.360 --> 00:44:20.760
is so lackluster

00:44:20.760 --> 00:44:22.880
that I don't think I can put it on the essential games list

00:44:22.880 --> 00:44:25.840
just for that. It does get some style points though

00:44:25.840 --> 00:44:28.360
for all of these other ideas of pinball created,

00:44:28.360 --> 00:44:30.680
and I would have liked to have seen it take that further.

00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:35.280
It seems weird that battle pinball can really just be,

00:44:35.520 --> 00:44:37.000
well, how many sets do you want to play?

00:44:37.160 --> 00:44:38.560
Like maybe they should have played around more

00:44:38.560 --> 00:44:39.940
with the idea of competition

00:44:39.940 --> 00:44:41.600
or what that could have been

00:44:41.600 --> 00:44:43.960
if they really wanted to stretch that mode out.

00:44:44.140 --> 00:44:44.980
A little more of that,

00:44:45.040 --> 00:44:46.580
and maybe we'd be talking about something,

00:44:46.800 --> 00:44:48.920
but because this is all there is,

00:44:48.920 --> 00:44:50.780
I don't think it's on the essential games list.

00:44:51.200 --> 00:44:54.980
Joe? I honestly don't have too much to say about this one.

00:44:56.340 --> 00:44:57.540
Like you said,

00:44:57.700 --> 00:45:01.400
the main pinball game mode

00:45:02.280 --> 00:45:03.360
is pretty generic.

00:45:03.580 --> 00:45:05.360
It's a generic, as far as I know,

00:45:05.460 --> 00:45:06.720
pretty generic form of pinball.

00:45:06.940 --> 00:45:08.300
I do like the variations.

00:45:08.740 --> 00:45:11.680
They're neat. They can be kind of fun in some instances.

00:45:11.820 --> 00:45:13.280
Other instances, they're a little pointless.

00:45:15.660 --> 00:45:17.620
I definitely don't think this is essential.

00:45:17.940 --> 00:45:19.660
Maybe if you're a pinball enthusiast,

00:45:19.680 --> 00:45:23.880
it's a curio that you might want to take a look at,

00:45:23.940 --> 00:45:28.040
but I wouldn't say that it's essential in any world.

00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:32.540
Sean? My biggest question with this game

00:45:32.540 --> 00:45:34.500
is why do they call it Rockin' Ball?

00:45:34.500 --> 00:45:36.820
I get that they changed the theme

00:45:36.820 --> 00:45:39.580
of the single-player board,

00:45:40.240 --> 00:45:42.060
the only single-player board,

00:45:42.160 --> 00:45:44.980
that's trying to just be pinball,

00:45:45.160 --> 00:45:47.200
into a kind of,

00:45:47.200 --> 00:45:48.600
sort of, vanilla,

00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:50.660
50s rock.

00:45:51.320 --> 00:45:55.660
Those are what the little icons are.

00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:58.040
But it's the only thing

00:45:58.040 --> 00:45:59.460
that has anything to do with rock.

00:45:59.640 --> 00:46:01.180
It had me questioning,

00:46:01.180 --> 00:46:02.580
why is this called Rockin' Ball?

00:46:02.580 --> 00:46:04.240
I was like, oh, because it's like kind of,

00:46:04.320 --> 00:46:06.740
you know, it's kind of rock-themed,

00:46:06.840 --> 00:46:09.580
but not really. And it's like one little mode.

00:46:09.760 --> 00:46:12.260
Like, it should have just been called Battle Pinball

00:46:12.260 --> 00:46:14.120
or keep the family pinball name.

00:46:14.160 --> 00:46:17.500
And that's really my biggest problem with this game

00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:19.040
is the naming convention.

00:46:19.520 --> 00:46:21.800
It wasn't interesting enough

00:46:21.800 --> 00:46:24.420
to call itself that.

00:46:25.300 --> 00:46:28.720
I mean, I had some fun with the multiplayer modes,

00:46:29.580 --> 00:46:31.940
but yeah, also it's not essential.

00:46:32.580 --> 00:46:34.960
Are all the characters that you can play as,

